  <section|Source pin and exact public route><label|source-pin-and-exact-public-route>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Public full-volume endpoint: <verbatim|YM.FullVolume.Final.july>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Finale/Program.lean>; it calls
    <verbatim|Campaign.operaShip>, constructs <verbatim|Jewel> through
    <verbatim|jewelOf17>, and uses <verbatim|Run.again> for the selected
    <verbatim|Spec.Final> witnesses.

    <item>The selected <verbatim|Spec.Final> chain reaches
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG17/Joint.lean>. It explicitly obtains <verbatim|hs :=
    grilled C hF hS hq s.copies>, where <verbatim|s.copies> is the selected
    <verbatim|CellHyp>; this is passed into the selected
    <verbatim|Pert.Supplier>.

    <item>Actual <verbatim|Org.Grill> producer:
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.grilled>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/South/FinalG.lean>. For each grade and
    requested depth it chooses a finite open station beyond the requested
    depth and all finitely many reference depths. It obtains a real
    <verbatim|Origin> receipt for every entitled field using
    <verbatim|inTime>, forms the corresponding <verbatim|Maker>, and applies
    <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Maker.patrons> to obtain the public
    pair-comparison grid. This is the public path; the alternative
    <verbatim|Study>/<verbatim|Furnace> constructors are not used here.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Mathematical correspondence><label|mathematical-correspondence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|lem:ex-public-frame-recovery> corresponds to
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.dials> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/South/Dine.lean>. Source notation: finite
    frame <verbatim|Size.axis>, approximate matrix <verbatim|(X.tone
    k).index>, selected Wilson transfer <verbatim|factory.terminal>, and the
    coefficient cost <verbatim|2 exp(columnLogs k) * coeffSize L>. The
    perturbation bound is per frame vector, at most <verbatim|1/4>; the
    manuscript proves invertibility by <verbatim|\|\|v-Av\|\|_1 \<less\>=
    \|\|v\|\|_1/4>, and the weaker source constant 2 follows.

    <item>The source <verbatim|dine> has a complex output.
    <verbatim|lens_supply> sums the finite <verbatim|cameras> bounds;
    <verbatim|embrace> supplies the corrected Wilson coefficient with its
    exponential-entry, forced-mode, and quarter-bias identities;
    <verbatim|dials> performs the finite-frame recovery; <verbatim|backTo>
    transports the local approximants; <verbatim|quakes> uses migration,
    occupancy, Drake separation, integrability, and the marked-copy estimate;
    <verbatim|root_sum> proves the finite root-test sum estimate. The exact
    realification is <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.realityC> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/South/FinalG.lean>: it uses the star-reality
    identity for the target insertion, the real-part projection, conjugation
    invariance of <verbatim|rootTest>, and the triangle inequality. In the
    manuscript, <verbatim|prop:ex-public-origin> proves the realification and
    linear-sum arithmetic conditional on the local coordinate approximation,
    support-transport, chamber-interior, and rooted-error receipts. Those
    receipts are not proved by this proposition.

    <item><verbatim|lem:ex-public-radial-choice> is the final threshold
    selection in <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.inTime>, using
    <verbatim|stockK>, <verbatim|gainChart>, and <verbatim|columnLogs_le>.
    The scale assumptions written in the manuscript are the exact asymptotic
    form needed for its product to tend to zero; the source derivation is by
    its <verbatim|Slow> product/sink estimate and the negative-flight bound.
    Accumulated column-log subpower is separately treated in
    <verbatim|ex-column-subpower> in the parent manuscript.

    <item>The exact output type assembled in <verbatim|thm:ex-public-grill>
    is <verbatim|OS.Grid.Covering.Works> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Phase/Approx.lean>).
    Its plots are differences of real approximants to the complex
    unreflected/reflected whole-word products. Pair targets are the real
    parts of complex product integrals, as in <verbatim|Maker.layout_hyp>; no
    invalid identity between real parts of factors and real parts of their
    products is used. The <verbatim|Works> control quantifiers use the fused
    mesh/period filter, while pair receipts fix approximation index first,
    then require all sufficiently large translations, and then an
    <verbatim|f.late> mesh and period set. Its smallness tends to zero in the
    approximation index, not in the extraction order.
    <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Maker.patrons>
    (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Cover.lean>) obtains the four pair
    receipts (plain/plain, plain/reflected, reflected/plain,
    reflected/reflected) by <verbatim|layout_hyp>, then uses
    <verbatim|receipt_sub> and the four-term expansion. The manuscript proves
    the finite arithmetic from these exact receipts; it keeps the four local
    pair receipts as explicit hypotheses.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Phase.replicas/seats> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/Phase/Seats.lean> proves a separate all-copy
    rooted power bound from <verbatim|C.Makes>, hierarchy, point limits, and
    <verbatim|CellHyp>. It is not an additional input to the public
    <verbatim|grilled> call above. It is therefore not asserted as a missing
    producer or silently used by this chapter.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Whole-word receipt proof added in this
  snapshot><label|whole-word-receipt-proof-added-in-this-snapshot>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Lemma <verbatim|lem:ex-public-replace-word> is the ordinary finite
    telescoping argument behind <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.replace_all>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Layout.lean>. Its sole non-elementary
    input is the planted product inequality supplied by the same-period
    <verbatim|Seam> in <verbatim|CellHyp.all>: for an injective cell
    assignment and local-cone factors, the absolute expectation of the copied
    product is bounded by the product of rooted tests. Each telescoping
    summand contains one replacement difference with cost
    <verbatim|costHint(k)> and <verbatim|n-1> factors with cost at most
    <verbatim|M>, giving exactly <verbatim|n*costHint(k)*M^(n-1)>. The proof
    includes the zero-length case separately. Integrability is assumed for
    the displayed finite products, as in the source's local-cone
    integrability lemma.

    <item>The source's preceding single-word input is
    <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Maker.nearby>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Atom.lean>. It sums centered baseline
    costs and purchase cash over the finite signed and reflected spin frame,
    moves the purchases to a centered cell by the real copy operation, and
    uses the family action to identify the copied baseline with the requested
    insertion. It requires the individual <verbatim|Origin> receipts (from
    the selected <verbatim|inTime> route) and <verbatim|CellHyp> centered
    bounds. These are still inputs; this chapter does not prove their
    upstream producer.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Maker.precise> applies the replacement
    estimate to the finite slot list after <verbatim|nearby>, giving a
    mesh/period-uniform product discrepancy. <verbatim|Maker.layout_hyp>
    concatenates the two word lists. For all large offsets the translated
    union is injective, and at a sufficiently fine period it remains
    injective on the torus; applying <verbatim|precise> to this union and
    taking the real part yields one pair receipt. The four choices
    (unreflected/reflected on each side) give the four receipts consumed by
    <verbatim|Maker.patrons>. Those finite assembly steps are proved in Lean
    and the manuscript theorem above gives their exact finite-sum arithmetic;
    the local <verbatim|Origin> estimates remain the analytic boundary.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Remaining mathematical inputs><label|remaining-mathematical-inputs>

  The selected-history construction still needs an ordinary-math translation
  of these substantive estimates rather than a mere declaration
  correspondence:

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|Scrim> plus the selected growth/budget records produce
    the real local approximants and their finite coefficient corrections
    (<verbatim|antilles>, <verbatim|embrace>, <verbatim|keys>,
    <verbatim|dials>).

    <item>The marked-copy price and migration/occupancy estimates produce the
    <verbatim|Served>/<verbatim|Vault> pair bounds used by <verbatim|quakes>
    (<verbatim|desal>, <verbatim|pollinate>, <verbatim|window>,
    <verbatim|toasted>, <verbatim|spiker>). The selected <verbatim|Origin>
    producer has not yet been translated into complete ordinary mathematics.

    <item>The same-law pair comparison from <verbatim|Origin> receipts is
    proved by the local replacement and finite assembly steps above; only
    their upstream <verbatim|Origin> inputs remain open.

    <item>The public positioned-correlations theorem also consumes a distinct
    full-mesh Cauchy receipt. This chapter does not subsume that premise.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Selected one-scale interpolation added in this
  snapshot><label|selected-one-scale-interpolation-added-in-this-snapshot>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|lem:ex-selected-cone-step> is the actual one-transition
    inequality used inside <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Renaissance.repriseQ>, not
    a replacement for the parent\<#2019\>s global discounted cone proof. It
    specializes the exact direction data in <verbatim|YM.Bid.direction>
    (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Loan.lean>) and proves the three conclusions used
    by the selected transition: the coarse remainder charge is bounded by the
    coarse columns times the core readout; the fine readout is bounded by the
    fine columns times the new readout; and the new readout is bounded by
    fine columns times the block volume and the old readout. The proof is the
    <verbatim|lead_bounds> perturbation argument in
    <verbatim|YM.Work.G08.cone_step> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/G08.lean>): bank
    gives <verbatim|2K barunit (1+s)\<leq\>1>, so twice the price times the
    direction error is dominated by the grade-weighted core; applying the
    perturbation estimate both before and after deleting the unit coordinate
    gives the two-sided readout bounds; <verbatim|4K\<twosuperior\>\<leq\>columns_i>
    and <verbatim|2K\<leq\>columns_{i+1}> pay the remainder and coordinate
    bounds. <verbatim|roomCost>, <verbatim|Bank>, and schedule slow-growth
    are required, not derived in this unit.

    <item><verbatim|prop:ex-selected-interpolation> follows the selected
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Renaissance.repriseQ> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Renaissance.lean>. For every coordinate
    basis vector it starts with the fine voice play at the inverse-readout
    coordinate, obtains an elementary coupon, and transports it through every
    signed motion/conjugation address by the centered reorientation receipt
    <verbatim|YM.Planned.GuardedAtom.audition_receipt>
    (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Planned/ATOM_GUARDED_LAYOUT/Orbit.lean>). The
    transported output has the transformed coefficient, danced transition
    density, same paid remainder and two Tale budgets on the image wing.

    <item>The single common linear coefficient is then the finite pencil
    <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.pencil> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/SOURCE_HISTORIES/Pencil.lean>)
    with weights <verbatim|chips(F, oldReadout(v))> and the transported
    columns. The manuscript derives the exact coefficient reconstruction from
    the normalized motion average; finite triangle estimates give the lead
    price. The weighted remainder price is <verbatim|residual_bill> in
    <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Motion> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/SOURCE_HISTORIES/Replay.lean>),
    whose proof uses the weighted orbit estimate <verbatim|vowel_tab>. The
    exact density identity is <verbatim|field_same> in
    <verbatim|Rebase.lean>, applied to the integrable linear transition of
    the heard density. <verbatim|pencil_cost>, <verbatim|pencil_density>, and
    <verbatim|pencil_ledger> then provide formatting, density, and linear
    profile fields. The new readout is injective by the fine-to-coarse
    estimate just proved; finite dimension makes it an isomorphism. The cone
    step also gives the new charge bound. Summing the finite transported Tale
    witnesses gives the exact two output budgets. No compactness,
    subsequence, or independent coefficient choices are involved.

    <item>The elementary coupons are not asserted without their producers.
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Meringue.single>
    (<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Meringue.lean>) assembles the principal,
    regular, and forced atom coupons by dominated absolute summation and
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Sonata.coupons> / <verbatim|Tale.upon>
    (<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Sonata.lean>). Its principal clause at each
    nonunit basis vector is <verbatim|Stampede.main>; source-chain tracking
    finds it still open pending the small primary-card/budget-card
    comparison. Its regular clause is <verbatim|Stampede.regular> and still
    requires the small-support, vanishing-jet regular-card estimate. The
    forced clause is supplied by the large projection estimate once the
    forced allowance is at most one and the keeper covers all nonzero forced
    slots. The parent\<#2019\>s <verbatim|sec:projection-payment-producer>
    proves the marked coefficient/profile payment but does not prove the open
    main or regular clauses. The necessary exact three-component Stampede
    inputs remain explicit in the TeX.

    <item>The full public use is <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Largo.compose>
    (<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Largo.lean>): finite reverse induction
    calls the interpolation to get each lower voice, then obtains its
    finite-wing tale and hence <verbatim|Carol> for the adjacent pair. The
    actual <verbatim|Tune>/<verbatim|Stampede> producer remains the stated
    analytic boundary; the finite interpolation does not close it by itself.

    <item>Parent canonical units already cover the separate signed comparison
    and global cone: <verbatim|sec:reference-difference> and
    <verbatim|sec:reference-cone> in the parent clone. This snapshot removed
    its duplicate attempt at those proofs.
  </itemize-minus>

  These are not claimed proved by the generic finite-sum lemmas alone. In
  particular, <verbatim|dine>'s calls to <verbatim|embrace> and
  <verbatim|quakes>, and <verbatim|Maker.patrons>' construction of
  <verbatim|precise>/<verbatim|layout_hyp> receipts, remain the substantive
  untranslated estimates in this unit. The current statements are conditional
  at exactly those boundaries.

