  <section|Corrected selected-interpolation
  audit><label|corrected-selected-interpolation-audit>

  The selected interpolation text now uses the actual finite Reynolds
  coefficient from <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Motion.chips>:
  <verbatim|share * scalar g (patch (backward g) v j)>. The manuscript writes
  this as <verbatim|chi_{g,j}(z)=\|Motion\|^{-1} sigma_g((g^{-1}z)_j)>,
  proves complex linearity by cancellation of the two conjugations, and sums
  each fixed-motion frame expansion to <verbatim|z/\|Motion\|>. It does not
  infer weighted estimates from an unweighted reconstruction bound. The
  displayed weighted coordinate identity uses <verbatim|core_axes>,
  <verbatim|core_tab>, and <verbatim|vowel_tab>; the unweighted bound uses
  <verbatim|patch_cost>.

  The paid lead input is motion-uniform by the exact <verbatim|PaidAtom>
  definition in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/SOURCE_HISTORIES/LocalDebt.lean>: for
  each reorientation it bounds the reoriented coefficient minus the
  reoriented lead. The proof uses that bound directly with the weighted
  core-axis identity; it does not treat motion as an isometry. The remainder
  charge is likewise attached to the original basis axis and uses the
  weighted vowel-axis estimate.

  Covariance conclusions are separated. <verbatim|Heard.travels> supplies
  density covariance; the forced-profile covariance is the <verbatim|Chorus>
  hypothesis; the exponential-entry covariance uses
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.chanting> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Jubilee.lean>,
  which uses soundness, lawfulness, and nonvanishing evaluation to subtract
  the forced dress from density and divide by evaluation. The prose only
  claims reindexing covariance of readout and profiles, not invariance of raw
  address arrays. The pointwise coefficient identity used in this step is the
  defining density decomposition, with the lawful dressing identity applied
  to its forced term.

