  <section|Public same-run Cauchy and positioned
  route><label|public-same-run-cauchy-and-positioned-route>

  The public point-Cauchy route is not <verbatim|FullVolume.Maintain.trained/invites/sweep>.
  The exact selected-run chain is:

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Campaign.sees> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Filled.lean> fixes one <verbatim|R>,
    campaign <verbatim|T>, winter <verbatim|H>, pillars <verbatim|W>, growth
    <verbatim|R.t>, and transfer tables <verbatim|R.stories>. It forms a
    <verbatim|Rising> witness from <verbatim|W.yields>,
    <verbatim|H.alignment>, and <verbatim|helmed>; the per-grade tenability
    fields use <verbatim|W.ports> and <verbatim|R.makes.calibrated>.

    <item>It applies <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.Rising.cinema>
    in <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Seat.lean> for a tuple in
    <verbatim|NoHit> with the Eves-ancestor property. Eventual
    <verbatim|Ponds>, Eves position/late-anchor properties, and all
    finite-label positive reserves are intersected once. The selected
    location map migrates by <verbatim|Eves.turns>. Its separation bound
    forces injectivity at the chosen rung: equality of two locations would
    make their separation zero while the positive squared budget is a lower
    bound. Injectivity gives occupancy one, which is bounded by the selected
    occupancy schedule.

    <item><verbatim|Rising.cinema> calls <verbatim|Rising.arrives> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Timber.lean>. The exact finite
    reduction is recorded in the manuscript: the paid allowance
    <verbatim|B_a> for label <verbatim|a> is converted to a positive marker
    weight <verbatim|x_a=\<zeta\>_a/(\|B_a\|+1)>, so <verbatim|x_a
    B_a\<leq\>\<zeta\>_a>; finite vault bounds are marched to a rung where
    the exponential grade budget diverges; the insertion comparison
    approximates the full pilot by a fixed-rung correlation; the latter is
    Cauchy by <verbatim|Rising.latter>; then the three-term triangle
    inequality proves pilot Cauchyness. <verbatim|YM.FullVolume.Sever.echoes>
    in <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Peat.lean> is the quantitative
    comparison: <verbatim|\<\|\|\>pilot\<minus\>Cresting_j\<\|\|\>\<leq\>refreeze/(brisk_j/2)>
    under its explicit vault, migration, occupancy, Drake, measurability, and
    same-history receipts.

    <item><verbatim|Rising.cinema> identifies the all-label census pilot
    exactly with the ordinary finite-volume Wilson observable by
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.Rising.absolute> in
    Seat.lean; no asymptotic or subsequence error is used in this
    identification.

    <item><verbatim|Campaign.purchased> then applies
    <verbatim|YM.Extraction.growFrom> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Extraction/Tame.lean>)
    to the dense ancestor subset of the open non-hit set, using
    <verbatim|sees> for pointwise Cauchy and the full-mesh oscillation
    receipt from <verbatim|YM.FullVolume.circulating>
    (<verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Region.lean>). The latter is proved from
    <verbatim|FixedBounds.localLip> and mesh spacing tending to zero. The
    finite-net argument in the TeX explains the upgrade from dense pointwise
    Cauchy to compact-uniform convergence along the full sequence.

    <item><verbatim|YM.FullVolume.Campaign.realUV> applies
    <verbatim|YM.FullVolume.positioned> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Profiles.lean>)
    to the same <verbatim|Purchased> family and <verbatim|FullVolume.genuine>
    bounds. The selected-run <verbatim|FullVolume.genuine> bounds are
    produced from <verbatim|R.makes> and <verbatim|R.financed>; the
    finite-difference chapter owns their detailed route. This delivers all
    fixed periods, word lists, and positioned derivatives on the full mesh.
  </enumerate>

  The excerpt translates the finite Cauchy reduction and spells out the
  full-mesh compact-open argument. It now proves the finite weighted-sum step
  from uniform confluence to the two <verbatim|Vault> inequalities and the
  Cauchy-disc estimate from support-price scaling, served transfer, and the
  integrated mode bound. It does not claim to independently reproduce every
  selected-history producer behind those receipts; in particular, the
  quantitative finite-menu response fields remain the explicit producer
  obligation in <verbatim|centered-construction>. This boundary matters:
  <verbatim|Campaign.sees> is the actual public same-history caller, whereas
  the <verbatim|Maintain> detector/sweep path is not.

  <section|Exact vault and insertion correspondence added in this
  snapshot><label|exact-vault-and-insertion-correspondence-added-in-this-snapshot>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.FullVolume.Retreat.Confluence> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Basin.lean> has two parts: eventual
    uniform boundedness over configurations and an eventual uniform Cauchy
    modulus. <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.Rising.hail> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Capital.lean> obtains this confluence
    for each scalar insertion and each box-marked insertion from fixed-rung
    branch stability. <verbatim|Rising.ships> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Timber.lean> calls
    <verbatim|limitVault>; its exact constants are finite sums of weights
    times the uniform bounds. <verbatim|lem:ex-uniform-confluence-vault>
    proves this price ledger directly and intersects the finite thresholds.

    <item>At the public call, <verbatim|Campaign.sees> passes the eventual
    pond package from <verbatim|Run.again(...).scrim.costs.pond>, positive
    <verbatim|\<zeta\>> tails, and <verbatim|p'\<geq\>1> from the same scrim.
    It passes the same history's <verbatim|Tenable>, paid credit, and
    migration fields. <verbatim|Eves.positions> supplies separation; equality
    of two positions contradicts its positive lower bound, so occupancy is at
    most one. Those are exactly the <verbatim|Rising.arrives> inputs used to
    choose the opened rung and later rung. <verbatim|Ponds.past> then
    constructs the per-label transition fields (<verbatim|Nectar>) from the
    pond's <verbatim|Brine>, <verbatim|Freightage>, <verbatim|Fiesta>,
    <verbatim|Cherry>, <verbatim|Banks>, footprint/camera bounds, and the
    listed occupancy, migration, Drake, soundness, and payment hypotheses.

    <item>In <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Sever.lean>, the
    <verbatim|Sever.worth>/<verbatim|Sever.incur> argument first turns Drake
    separation and the connected-halo packing bound into a cover lower bound
    for every active support. Multiplying its coefficient envelope by
    <verbatim|\|z\|\<leq\>exp(B/64)> is paid by lowering the support exponent
    by two. <verbatim|Sever.garnish> packages that estimate as a served
    field. <verbatim|Retain.waft> transports the served field down each
    transition: its exact pushed coefficient identity and unit-mass kernel
    preserve each mode integral by Fubini. <verbatim|Sever.charges> at the
    opened rung then applies the integrated-mode estimate
    <verbatim|ex-centered-sail> with the opened-rung vault. The manuscript
    expands these numerical steps; all names and paths are kept here for
    source audit only.

    <item>Fixed-rung Cauchyness is the selected <verbatim|Rising.latter>
    route, not the optional DCT condition stated as a generic sufficient
    criterion. It uses <verbatim|Rising.flooded> for <verbatim|Flux>,
    <verbatim|Rising.hail> for confluence, and
    <verbatim|Retreat.Confluence.laven> for the normalized moment. The
    source-side conditional boundary left in the manuscript is the production
    of the quantitative adjacent-scale response fields and their shared
    service-price estimates, not the finite-net, vault ledger, or Cauchy-disc
    arithmetic.
  </itemize-minus>

